WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:05.800
Our Universe was created about 13.8
billion years ago in the Big Bang.

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:09.440
At first, it was very simple,

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:12.240
consisting of little more
than hydrogen and helium

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:13.480
and lots of energy.

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:16.720
There were no stars or galaxies,

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:20.280
no planets
and certainly no living creatures.

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:24.840
Then, gradually,
more complex things appeared.

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:27.440
The first stars and galaxies

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:31.240
probably appeared within about
200 million years of the Big Bang.

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:37.440
As big stars lived and died, they
blew up and created new elements.

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:41.560
Those new elements allowed
the creation of new materials

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:44.840
such as the dust
and ice and rocks and minerals

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:46.360
from which planets are made.

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:51.840
Our Sun and solar system appeared
about 4.5 billion years ago,

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:54.320
and by 4 billion years ago,

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:56.800
it's likely that life
had emerged on Earth.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:00.040
Life evolved and diversified

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:04.080
but most of it consisted of tiny,
single-celled organisms

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:08.560
until, about 1 billion years ago, the
first many-celled organisms appeared.

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:12.000
From about five hundred
million years ago,

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:14.480
big creatures became
much more common,

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:19.360
from trilobites to trees
to tyrannosaurus rex.

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:24.120
The first humans
evolved very recently,

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:26.600
just about 200,000 years ago.

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:29.120
Though it wasn't obvious at the time,

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:32.840
the appearance of humans
turned out to be hugely important

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:36.840
because humans were able
to share ideas and information

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:40.760
better than any other species
that ever existed.

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:42.600
Using that ability,

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:46.320
our ancestors gradually
built up stores of information

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:48.720
that allowed them
to control their environments

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:50.360
more and more powerfully.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:55.080
The process accelerated until,
in just the last 100 years,

00:01:55.640 --> 00:02:00.640
we have become so powerful that
what we do in the next few decades

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:03.360
will determine the future
of the oceans,

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:06.520
the climate, and of most
other species on Earth,

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:08.920
including our own descendants.

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:15.000
Many scholars believe that this
represents a new geological epoch.

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:16.920
The Anthropocene.

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:20.440
In the last 50 years,

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:24.640
we humans have begun to control
energy and resources

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:28.800
on such a vast scale
that we are transforming the land,

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:32.240
the seas and the atmosphere
of the Earth.

00:02:33.080 --> 00:02:37.120
So, planet Earth is at a turning
point in its history.

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:40.400
Humans, now the dominant species,

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:43.840
will either lead the biosphere
towards a flourishing future,

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:46.200
or to catastrophe.

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:48.560
Perhaps triggered by nuclear wars

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:51.840
that could ruin swathes
of the planet in just a few hours,

00:02:52.280 --> 00:02:56.920
or caused more slowly by the
continued release of greenhouse gases

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:58.640
until the land is flooded

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:01.800
and global climates
are too hot to grow enough food.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:08.880
Never before has a single species

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:11.640
determined the future
of the entire biosphere.

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:16.080
The good news is that we
understand the science,

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:18.560
and we already have
many of the technologies needed

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:20.280
to build a sustainable future.

00:03:21.160 --> 00:03:24.640
What’s missing now
is the political technology.

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:27.640
How can governments and peoples

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:30.840
be encouraged to see the challenges
that they all share,

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:34.880
rather than simply defending their
own local and immediate interests?

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:41.840
Only by collaboration can we avoid
the many dangers we face today.

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:53.880
Can we steer planet Earth towards
a prosperous future in which humans

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:58.640
and all the other organisms on which
we depend can flourish for thousands,

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:02.880
even perhaps, for millions
of years into the future?

